{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Handoff state. Change 1919 patch set 2 (commit 78c9cce398) is the current, complete implementation; every local gate is green (make lint, make typecheck, tests/unit 11290 passed, tests/scripts 1046, tests/interfaces+tests/lib 1932, plus the file's own 18 tests). Gerrit shows LLM-Review/Verified/Code-Review all pending on PS2 and unresolved=0. The blocker is GitHub Actions runner starvation in navapbc/rebar: the two Gerrit Verified Gate runs for this change (32306779189, 32306986850) have sat 'queued' for hours, as has every unrelated workflow in the repo (Reconciler Heartbeat Canary, Test Suite (mirror)). The one Verified-1 on record is against PS1 and is NOT a test verdict — the bot's own message says its jobs were CANCELLED, which is what an upload of PS2 does to the superseded PS1 run. No recheck was issued (nothing failed; a recheck only enqueues another job behind the same stalled pool) and nothing was forced. NEXT STEPS for whoever resumes: wait for the runner pool to recover, confirm LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 on PS2 with no unresolved comments, Submit, then close this ticket from a worktree fast-forwarded onto the merged commit (rebar transition unaroused-undead-ibisbill in_progress closed). Worktree /Users/joeoakhart/ci-gate-compat-6f2e is left intact on branch ci-gate-compat-6f2e."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787177220806855001,"uuid":"4da23bbb-3e88-483a-a85e-565e04347e3a"}